#!/usr/bin/env rexx
/*
   Name:     "HelloWorld_newLogic.rxj"

   Invoke:   "rexx HelloWorld_newLogic.rxj"
                or
             "rexxj HelloWorld_newLogic.rxj" (Windows)
                or
             "rexxj.sh HelloWorld_newLogic.rxj" (Unix)

   Purpose:  create a window with a choice-object and two text-fields and buttons;
             if the ok-button is pressed then popup another window and display what
             was chosen and entered.

             This version stresses Object Rexx and the wrapper class "BSF.CLS" which
             makes Java look like if it was Object Rexx ...
             ;)

             -> demonstrate how one can forgoe the old BSF "addEventListener" for
                the new synchroneous event listeners

   Needs:    ooRexx, BSF4Rexx

   Date:    2009-10-18

   Changes: 2010-02-10, rgf, add a small sleeping time before exiting Rexx; this way
                        pending Java callbacks to Rexx event handlers can be serviced

   Author:   Rony G. Flatscher, University of Essen, WU Wien University,
             derived from Peter Kalender's proof-of-concept work for the "Essener Ski Seminar",
             University of Essen (Oct 2000 to Feb 2001)


   last change: $Revision$ $Author$ $Date$

   license:

    ------------------------ Apache Version 2.0 license -------------------------
       Copyright (C) 2001-2010 Rony G. Flatscher

       Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
       you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
       You may obtain a copy of the License at

           http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

       Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
       distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
       WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
       See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
       limitations under the License.
    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

if      BsfInvokedBy()=1 then say "This Rexx program was invoked by Java!"
else if BsfInvokedBy()=2 then say "This Rexx program was invoked by Rexx, JVM loaded by Rexx!"
else                          say "No JVM present, we got troubles ..."

         /* create an event handler object  */
eh=.eventHandler~new

         /* create a RexxProxy to serve two Java listeners  */
proxy=BsfCreateRexxProxy(eh, , "java.awt.event.ActionListener", "java.awt.event.WindowListener")

         /* create a Java awt window and a Java awt button       */
tmpWin = .awtFrame~new('Hello World!')
tmpWin~addWindowListener(proxy)        -- add our event handler to button


.bsf~bsf.import("java.awt.Button", "awtButton")     /* another way to define a Java class   */
tmpBut = .awtButton~new('Press me!')
tmpBut~addActionListener(proxy)        -- add our event handler to button

         /* prepare window and show it, using cascading messages (two twiddles '~')   */
tmpWin ~~add(tmpBut) ~~pack ~~show ~~toFront

say "waiting for exit..."
eh~waitForExit    /* waits on a control variable to be changed to .true (see implementation below) */
say "wait is over: now exiting Rexx."

tmpWin~dispose    /* dispose frame  */
call SysSleep .1  /* let Java close gracefully, allow Rexx event handlers to be present for Java callbacks */


::REQUIRES BSF.CLS    -- requires the BSF-class

        /* one way, how to define a Java class in Object Rexx   */
::CLASS "awtFrame" SUBCLASS bsf
::METHOD init
  self~init:super('java.awt.Frame', ARG(1, 'A'))


/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
::CLASS "eventHandler"
::method init                    -- set bExitProgram attribute to .false
  expose bExitProgram
  bExitProgram=.false

::method unknown                 -- do nothing if other events are raised
  use arg methName, args
  -- uncomment the following line to see the unhandled events
  -- say "unknown: method="pp(methName) "eventObject="pp(args[1]~toString)

::method windowClosing           -- clear bExitProgram attribute
  expose bExitProgram
  bExitProgram=.true

::method actionPerformed         -- clear bExitProgram attribute
  expose bExitProgram
  bExitProgram=.true

::method waitForExit             -- wait for bExitProgram attribute to gain a specific value
  expose bExitProgram

  guard on when bExitProgram=.true
  say "waitForExit, lock released, returning ..."